>>- There are a few commands that are redundant; the way they've evolved
>>	there's no real reason to keep them separate.
>>	For example, . and s both cause waiting - is there any
>>		reason you wouldn't want to search while waiting?

>Maybe just waiting should cost less food (50%) and speed up your
>regeneration of lost hitpoints and energy. This would be logic: while
>waiting in stead of searching or doing something else, you don't use up
>that much energy.

In Moria, it works this way.  Hit points and mana regenerate at double the
normal rate, and food consumption is reduced by 1 point per turn (normal
consumption is 2 per turn, but some items affect that).  Also, in Moria,
monsters are much less likely to wake up when you are resting than when you
are doing something else.

There is one essential difference between resting in Moria and in Nethack.
In Moria, it is something you do all the time; there is no shortage of
food, so you will always rest after a tough combat or after casting several
spells.  In Nethack, doubling the rate of regeneration while you are
resting might unbalance the game, because it would greatly reduce food
shortages.  

Disclaimer:  I am a Moria wizard, but I haven't played Nethack very much.
